WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.333
UX friction is silently killing products.

2
00:00:08.333 --> 00:00:14.000
It's the reason people abandon apps they actually wanted to use.

3
00:00:19.333 --> 00:00:25.000
Friction is any point where the experience feels harder than it should.

4
00:00:25.167 --> 00:00:30.667
Any moment of hesitation. Any unnecessary step. Any confusion.

5
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:41.000
Four types: Cognitive, Physical, Emotional, and Temporal.

6
00:00:41.333 --> 00:00:47.333
Cognitive: too many choices, unclear labels. Brain works too hard.

7
00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:52.667
Temporal: too slow, too many steps for something simple.

8
00:00:53.333 --> 00:00:59.333
Amazon 1-click checkout removed payment friction entirely.

9
00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:04.667
Every extra step costs conversions. Every confusing label costs users.

10
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:08.667
Learn UX design at 0xverse Academy.

